---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A banner is a full-width message at the top of the app or a page, about something that stays true
  until it changes: a maintenance window, a trial that is ending, a lost connection. Put it above the
  content, edge to edge, and show one at a time.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-banner headline='New dashboard'>Your reports moved to the new dashboard.</wc-banner>
    <wc-banner intent='info' headline='Scheduled maintenance'>
      The service is unavailable on Friday from 22:00 to 23:00 UTC.
      <wc-button slot='action' variant='text' size='sm'>Status page</wc-button>
    </wc-banner>
    <wc-banner intent='warning' headline='Your trial ends in 3 days.'>
      Upgrade to keep your projects.
      <wc-button slot='action' variant='text' size='sm'>Compare plans</wc-button>
      <wc-button slot='action' variant='filled' size='sm'>Upgrade</wc-button>
    </wc-banner>
    <wc-banner intent='danger' headline='Connection lost.'>
      Changes are saved on this device until you are back online.
    </wc-banner>
    <wc-banner intent='success' headline='Payment received.'>Thank you.</wc-banner>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Banner, alert or snackbar</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Banner</strong>: about the whole app or page, true until something changes. Full width,
    above the content, stays until the condition ends or the person dismisses it.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong><a href='/components/alert'><code>wc-alert</code></a></strong>: about one part of the
    content, shown in place beside it.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong><a href='/components/snackbar'><code>wc-snackbar</code></a></strong>: brief feedback on
    something the person just did; it floats and goes away by itself.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
  The banner uses the alert's vocabulary: <code>intent</code> (neutral when unset), <code>headline</code>,
  the message in the default slot or <code>description</code>, <code>icon</code>, and one or two buttons
  in the <code>action</code> slot. Narrow banners wrap the actions onto their own line.
</p>
